From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:00:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/38] rust: fs: DAX for file systems whose data lives in a
 physical window

For a file system whose bytes sit at physical addresses outside the page
cache, such as memory a hypervisor shares with the guest: fs::dax gives
the range struct pages (Window, over memremap_pages), a dax_device over
it (Device, with direct_access as plain arithmetic), an iomap
Operations trait answering 'this file range is at that window offset',
and read, write and mmap entry points that hand the work to dax_iomap_rw
and dax_iomap_fault. Faults are served under the mapping's invalidate
lock and retry on EAGAIN, as fuse's DAX does; break_layout waits for
users of a range before the window behind it is reused.

file::Operations gains read_iter, write_iter, mmap and fsync, each
handed the typed inode alongside the untyped file. inode::New::set_dax
marks an inode DAX, INode gets set_size and truncate_pages, Lockable
gains a WriteSem for the exclusive inode lock, address_space::Ops::dax
is the no-op table a DAX inode needs, and VmaNew::set_ops installs
fault handlers.

